# Build output and dependencies: regenerated inside the image, never needed
# from the context. The ** forms are the root-context equivalent of the old
# app-level ignores: a bare name in .dockerignore only matches the context
# root, and every workspace has its own node_modules and dist.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Git, CI and local tooling
.git/
.github/
**/.atl/

# Docs and design artifacts not used at runtime
**/*.md
**/skills-lock.json
**/odd/

# Logs and foreign lockfiles (these projects are bun-locked)
**/*.log
package-lock.json

# Env files never enter the context or an image; the negation mirrors the
# root .gitignore so the env.example template stays available.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
